The current rule is: **wilds are only created from winning lines of exactly 3 symbols**, not 4 or 5.

So your bottom row with 4 matching triangles paid as a win, but **did not spawn a wild by design**.

```595:610:AXEL/axel_project/combat/scripts/combat_root.gd
func _resolve_lines_impl(lines: Array) -> void:
	var to_clear: Dictionary = {}
	var wild_spawns: Dictionary = {}
	for line in lines:
		var cells: Array = line["cells"]
		for p in cells:
			to_clear[p] = true
		if int(line["length"]) == 3:
			var mid: Vector2i = cells[1]
			wild_spawns[mid] = true
	var all_cleared: Array = to_clear.keys()
	grid.clear_cells_and_emit(all_cleared)
	for p in wild_spawns.keys():
		if grid.get_cell(p) == null:
			grid.set_cell(p, wild_symbol)
```

And the test suite explicitly checks this behavior (3-line spawns, 5-line does not add extra spawn behavior):

```190:219:AXEL/axel_project/combat/test/princess_check.gd
func _assert_wild_spawn_only_on_3_line() -> void:
	# Exactly three in a row => one line of length 3 => wild at middle cell.
	...
	var line_wilds := _count_wilds(cr)
	if line_wilds < 1:
		push_error("Expected at least one wild spawn from a length-3 line.")
	...
	var line5_wilds := _count_wilds(cr2)
	if line5_wilds > line_wilds:
		push_error("5-line should not create additional wild spawn behavior.")
```

For the “original Moon Princess files” in this repo: the exported `moon_princess_files` folder appears to be styling/paytable assets, not core game logic scripts. But your own combat design/implementation docs state this same MP-style rule: **3-only wild spawn, middle cell; no spawn for 4/5**.

